id: pm-slack-v524
title: Adopt --respect-item-release in changelog scripts and close the shipped-but-stale Block Kit truncation tracker
description: "Adopts pm-changelog 2026.7.24 --respect-item-release across the changelog scripts and bumps the devDependency, then uses the new capability to close pm-slack-gx2h, whose fix shipped in v2026.06.07 but whose tracker stayed open because closing it would have retro-dated the work into the current release window."
type: Chore
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: changelog,fleet-consistency,release-hygiene
created_at: "2026-07-24T21:36:30.418Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-24T21:43:12.785Z"
assignee: claude
author: claude
acceptance_criteria: "all four changelog scripts pass --respect-item-release; pm-changelog devDependency is ^2026.7.24; pm-slack-gx2h is closed and appears under the 2026.6.7 heading not Unreleased; changelog:check green"
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-24T21:36:31.097Z",claude,"Verified with the published pm-changelog 2026.7.24: pm-slack-gx2h attributes to the 2026.6.7 heading and changelog:check exits 0. Underlying fix independently re-verified before closing — 60/60 unit tests assert the 3000/150 limits against oversized inputs, and a live 6000-char notify produced a 149-char ellipsised header with 0 limit violations across 14 blocks in the notify and digest payloads."
  "2026-07-24T21:43:12.784Z",claude,"Greptile review finding adopted: the daily release workflow invokes pm-changelog DIRECTLY (npx pm-changelog, three times) rather than through the npm scripts, so patching only package.json left the generation path that actually produces the published CHANGELOG.md and RELEASE_NOTES.md without the flag while release:check validated with it. Added --respect-item-release to all three release.yml invocations so generation and validation agree. YAML re-validated."
body: ""
